{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' generate-plan.sh\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nskill=\"/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T121358Z-current-fresh6/current/worker/planning\"\nfinal_plan=\"basic-test-proof-current-20260811T121358Z-current-fresh6-isolated-plan\"\nplan=\"basic-test-proof-current-20260811t121358z-current-fresh6-isolated-plan\"\nexport PLANS_ROOT=\"/tmp/current-fresh6/current/workspace\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/create-plan.sh\" \"$plan\" \"Button chain HTML implementation proof\"\nmv \"$plan\" \"$final_plan\"\nplan=\"$final_plan\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$plan\" current-state \\\n  -p 2.1: \"The isolated benchmark workspace contains the prompt, benchmark instructions, task specification, and session-id.txt. This proof plans the future creation of button-chain.html only; no HTML artifact, browser session, server, driver, or execution tooling is used during planning.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$plan\" desired-outcome \\\n  -p 3.1: \"A future executor can create button-chain.html with one initial button, append exactly one button below the current last button when that last button is pressed, clear the document when the fourth generated button is pressed, and display the exact lowercase text finished with a visible white border.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$plan\" approach \\\n  -p 4.1: \"The plan separates the HTML subtree, delegated click handling, completion branch, completion style, static review, and final UI story verification into atomic work units. Verification is planned but not executed in this proof.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$plan\" scope \\\n  -p 5.1: \"In scope is one standalone file named button-chain.html and the acceptance evidence needed to verify its button-chain behavior later. Out of scope for this proof is creating, editing, opening, serving, inspecting, or testing any HTML.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$plan\" affected-areas \\\n  -p 6.1: \"The future affected area is button-chain.html, including the #button-chain-root markup subtree, button-chain click handling code, completion code, and .completion-message styling. The current planning proof affects only Markdown plan artifacts in this plan directory.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$plan\" constraints-and-decisions \\\n  -p 7.1: \"The benchmark must use only the tagged repository-local planning skill and relative references under the rendered worker capsule. The plan remains in the isolated workspace, uses helper-created planning artifacts, and records telemetry as unavailable because reading Codex SQLite stores outside BENCH_ROOT and the tagged capsule is outside the declared filesystem boundary.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$plan\" risks-and-open-questions \\\n  -p 8.1: \"The main execution risk is off-by-one ambiguity around generated buttons. This plan defines generated button one as the first button appended after pressing the initial button, so pressing generated button four triggers the finished state.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/create-ui-validation.sh\" \"$plan\" \"Future local button-chain.html opened by browser verification after implementation; not opened during this planning proof.\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/add-goal.sh\" \"$plan\" 01-build-contract \"Build the button chain contract\" \"button-chain.html has the planned static structure, behavior logic, completion branch, completion styling, and a static acceptance review ready before browser validation.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs \\\n  -p 2.1: \"No implementation file exists in this proof. The executor starts from the future requirement and must create button-chain.html as a standalone document.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract why-needed \\\n  -p 4.1: \"This goal owns the concrete file contract so the later UI story can verify behavior without adding unplanned implementation scope.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract scope \\\n  -p 5.1: \"Included are the initial button subtree, delegated button click logic, fourth-generated completion behavior, white-border finished state, and static acceptance review. Excluded are browser execution and any second file.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract affected-areas \\\n  -p 6.1: \"Future affected file is button-chain.html. Planned atomic targets are #button-chain-root, handleButtonClick, completeOnFourthGenerated, .completion-message, and a source-review verification flow.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract dependencies-and-handoffs \\\n  -p 7.1: \"This goal has no prerequisite goal. It hands button-chain.html and the static acceptance checklist to 02-validate-ui-story.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract implementation-risks-edge-cases \\\n  -p 8.1: \"Use event delegation or equivalent guarded logic so only the current last button is active for appending. Count only generated buttons, not the initial button, and clear the document before rendering the finished message.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --testing-requirement \"$plan\" 01-build-contract yes \"The goal changes user-visible markup, behavior, and style, so it owns a static verification work unit before final browser validation.\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/add-goal.sh\" \"$plan\" 02-validate-ui-story \"Validate the button chain UI story\" \"The planned browser user story proves the completed interaction: three generated appends occur one at a time, pressing the fourth generated button clears the document, and finished appears with a visible white border.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 02-validate-ui-story current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs \\\n  -p 2.1: \"This goal starts after 01-build-contract creates button-chain.html and completes the static acceptance review.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 02-validate-ui-story why-needed \\\n  -p 4.1: \"The future behavior is user-facing and must be verified through direct browser input, but this proof only records the story and run cache.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 02-validate-ui-story scope \\\n  -p 5.1: \"Included is one bounded browser story for the full button chain. Excluded during this proof is actually opening the HTML file or running browser automation.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 02-validate-ui-story affected-areas \\\n  -p 6.1: \"Verification target is the future rendered button-chain.html page through normal click input. No implementation target is changed by this goal.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 02-validate-ui-story dependencies-and-handoffs \\\n  -p 7.1: \"Depends on W01 through W05 from 01-build-contract. Completion hands off browser evidence, user story status, and any bug-register entries.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 02-validate-ui-story implementation-risks-edge-cases \\\n  -p 8.1: \"The browser story must click only the visible current last button in sequence and must reject states where earlier buttons append, more than one button appears per click, the text is not exactly finished, or the white border is not visible.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --testing-requirement \"$plan\" 02-validate-ui-story yes \"This goal is entirely verification and owns the required browser user-story proof.\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$plan\" W01 markup button-chain.html \"#button-chain-root\" N/A \"Create the standalone document body subtree with exactly one initial button visible at load.\" \"—\" 01-build-contract 01-step-initial-button-markup\n\"$skill/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$plan\" W02 source button-chain.html \"handleButtonClick\" N/A \"Add the click handler that appends exactly one generated button below the current last button and ignores non-last buttons for append behavior.\" \"W01\" 01-build-contract 02-step-last-button-append-logic\n\"$skill/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$plan\" W03 source button-chain.html \"completeOnFourthGenerated\" N/A \"Add the completion branch so pressing generated button four clears the document and renders the exact text finished.\" \"W02\" 01-build-contract 03-step-fourth-generated-completion\n\"$skill/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$plan\" W04 style button-chain.html \".completion-message\" N/A \"Style the finished state so the text finished has a visible white border.\" \"W03\" 01-build-contract 04-step-finished-border-style\n\"$skill/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$plan\" W05 verification N/A \"Static HTML acceptance review\" N/A \"Review the future button-chain.html source against the initial button, append, completion, exact text, and white-border contract before browser validation.\" \"W01,W02,W03,W04\" 01-build-contract 05-step-static-acceptance-review\n\"$skill/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$plan\" W06 verification N/A \"US-01 browser button-chain flow\" N/A \"Run the future browser story that clicks the current last button until completion and records pass or bug evidence.\" \"W01,W02,W03,W04,W05\" 02-validate-ui-story 01-step-browser-button-chain-story\n\n\"$skill/scripts/add-coverage.sh\" \"$plan\" \"Future file button-chain.html starts with exactly one visible initial button.\" W01 \"The markup work unit owns the initial DOM subtree.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/add-coverage.sh\" \"$plan\" \"Pressing the current last button appends exactly one generated button below it.\" W02,W05,W06 \"The source unit implements the append contract and both verification units check it.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/add-coverage.sh\" \"$plan\" \"Pressing generated button four clears the document.\" W03,W05,W06 \"The completion unit defines the fourth-generated branch and verification checks the resulting empty prior document state.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/add-coverage.sh\" \"$plan\" \"Completion prints exact lowercase text finished.\" W03,W05,W06 \"The completion branch owns the text and verification checks exact casing.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/add-coverage.sh\" \"$plan\" \"Completion text has a visible white border.\" W04,W05,W06 \"The style unit owns the border and verification checks visibility.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/add-coverage.sh\" \"$plan\" \"Planning proof contains no created, opened, served, inspected, or tested HTML.\" W05,W06 \"Both verification steps are planned instructions only in this proof.\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --decomposition-review \"$plan\" completed\n\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/01-step-initial-button-markup instructions \\\n  -p 5.1: \"When executing later, create button-chain.html as a standalone HTML document and define #button-chain-root as the only initial interactive subtree.\" \\\n  -p 5.2: \"Place exactly one initial button in #button-chain-root. Do not add generated buttons in initial markup.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/01-step-initial-button-markup acceptance-criteria \\\n  -p 6.1: \"A source review can identify one initial button and no generated buttons before any click.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/01-step-initial-button-markup 7.1 \"W02 can attach behavior to the initial button and the shared #button-chain-root container.\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/02-step-last-button-append-logic instructions \\\n  -p 5.1: \"When executing later, implement handleButtonClick so it first confirms the clicked button is the current last button in the chain.\" \\\n  -p 5.2: \"For eligible clicks before completion, append exactly one new generated button immediately below the previous last button and make that new button the only append-eligible last button.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/02-step-last-button-append-logic acceptance-criteria \\\n  -p 6.1: \"Each eligible click increases the button count by one, positions the new button below the previous last button, and earlier buttons do not append extra buttons.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/02-step-last-button-append-logic 7.1 \"W03 can rely on a generated-button counter that excludes the initial button.\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/03-step-fourth-generated-completion instructions \\\n  -p 5.1: \"When executing later, implement completeOnFourthGenerated so the fourth generated button is the completion trigger.\" \\\n  -p 5.2: \"On that trigger, clear the existing document content before rendering the completion message with exact lowercase text finished.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/03-step-fourth-generated-completion acceptance-criteria \\\n  -p 6.1: \"After generated button four is pressed, no chain buttons remain visible and the only completion text is exactly finished.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/03-step-fourth-generated-completion 7.1 \"W04 can target the rendered completion message through the .completion-message selector.\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/04-step-finished-border-style instructions \\\n  -p 5.1: \"When executing later, add .completion-message styling in button-chain.html only.\" \\\n  -p 5.2: \"Set a white border that remains visibly distinguishable around the finished text in the rendered completion state.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/04-step-finished-border-style acceptance-criteria \\\n  -p 6.1: \"The completion message has visible bordered styling whose border color is white.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/04-step-finished-border-style 7.1 \"W05 can inspect the source for the completion selector and white border declaration.\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/05-step-static-acceptance-review instructions \\\n  -p 5.1: \"When executing later, inspect only the completed button-chain.html source and compare it with W01 through W04.\" \\\n  -p 5.2: \"Record whether the initial state, append guard, generated-button count, completion clearing, exact finished text, and white border are all represented before browser verification starts.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/05-step-static-acceptance-review acceptance-criteria \\\n  -p 6.1: \"The static review records pass evidence for every acceptance item or opens a bug before W06 runs.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-build-contract/05-step-static-acceptance-review 7.1 \"W06 can run only after this review has no open implementation defect.\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 02-validate-ui-story/01-step-browser-button-chain-story instructions \\\n  -p 5.1: \"When executing later, open the local button-chain.html in a browser and use only direct clicks on the visible current last button.\" \\\n  -p 5.2: \"Click the initial button to create generated button one, then click the current last generated button until generated button four is pressed and completion appears.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$plan\" 02-validate-ui-story/01-step-browser-button-chain-story acceptance-criteria \\\n  -p 6.1: \"The story passes only if each pre-completion click appends exactly one button below the last button, pressing generated button four clears the document, and the page shows exact text finished with a visible white border.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 02-validate-ui-story/01-step-browser-button-chain-story 7.1 \"If the browser story fails, record a bugs.md row and create investigation and fix goals before retesting.\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/add-ui-story.sh\" \"$plan\" US-01 \"Local user starts from future button-chain.html with one visible initial button.\" \"Click the current last button four times in sequence, always selecting the newest visible last button after each append.\" \"Direct click input on the initial button, generated button one, generated button two, and generated button three or four according to the visible current last-button sequence.\" \"The first three completion-path clicks append exactly one button below the prior last button, the fourth generated-button press clears the document, and finished appears with a visible white border.\" W01,W02,W03,W04,W06\n\"$skill/scripts/configure-ui-story-cache.sh\" \"$plan\" US-01 \"Future local button-chain.html is loaded with exactly one initial button visible.\" \"Click sequence on the visible current last button.\" \"Initial button, then generated buttons in visible last-button order until the fourth generated button triggers completion.\" \"After each pre-completion click exactly one lower button appears; after completion exact text finished appears with a visible white border and no chain buttons remain.\" \"2 seconds per click readiness check\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan/01-build-contract\" 01-step-initial-button-markup \"Planned verification only. Inspect button-chain.html after implementation and confirm #button-chain-root contains exactly one initial button and no pre-rendered generated buttons. Do not run during this planning proof.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan/01-build-contract\" 02-step-last-button-append-logic \"Planned verification only. Inspect source and later browser behavior to confirm handleButtonClick accepts only the current last button and appends exactly one generated button per eligible click. Do not run during this planning proof.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan/01-build-contract\" 03-step-fourth-generated-completion \"Planned verification only. Inspect source and later browser behavior to confirm generated button four clears prior document content and renders exact lowercase text finished. Do not run during this planning proof.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan/01-build-contract\" 04-step-finished-border-style \"Planned verification only. Inspect .completion-message styling and later rendered output to confirm a visible white border surrounds finished. Do not run during this planning proof.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan/01-build-contract\" 05-step-static-acceptance-review \"Planned verification only. Complete a bounded static acceptance checklist against button-chain.html after implementation and before browser validation. Do not run during this planning proof.\"\n\"$skill/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan/02-validate-ui-story\" 01-step-browser-button-chain-story \"Planned browser verification only. Later, open button-chain.html and execute US-01 from ui-story-runs/US-01.md using direct clicks. Do not open or test HTML during this planning proof.\"\n\n\"$skill/scripts/create-progress.sh\" \"$plan/01-build-contract\" 01-build-contract\n\"$skill/scripts/create-progress.sh\" \"$plan/02-validate-ui-story\" 02-